## Breaking Down the Vulnerability Report
The report flagged several severe issues inside that old jQuery version:

* End-of-Life (EOL) Warning: Version 1.x is dead and no longer gets security updates.
* Prototype Pollution (CVE-2019-11358): Attackers can trick jQuery.extend() into modifying global JavaScript object properties, crashing the application or altering behavior.
* Cross-Site Scripting / XSS (CVE-2020-11022 & CVE-2020-11023): Malicious code sent inside simple HTML fragments passed to functions like .html() or .append() can run automatically in user browsers.

